# shir_nodes/repeat_str.node — expression-level semantic IR node.
# Repeat a string N times (lowered from `printf '%100s' '' | tr ' ' C`).
#
# Backends: Perl "C" x N, JS .repeat(), C memset, Rust repeat()
# Fallback: sh2.repeatStr(text, count)
#
# ShIR_TextOps_Strings proves `repeat_str_sound`: the loop-shaped definition is
# `concat (replicate count text)`, its length is `count * length text`, and the
# zero/one/empty-text cases are the identities the arms rely on. Emitted for the
# `yes X | head -n K` idiom, whose line terminator is part of `text`.

node RepeatStr
tag "RepeatStr"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field text: expr
field count: expr
spec: TextOps#repeat_str_sound
